      "body": "Hey - I've found 1 issue\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n~~~markdown\nPlease address the comments from this code review:\n\n## Individual Comments\n\n### Comment 1\n<location path=\"reports.py\" line_range=\"24\" />\n<code_context>\n\n\n def schedule(db, report, scheduled_at):\n+    if scheduled_at < 0:\n+        raise ValueError(\"scheduled time must be non-negative\")\n     with db:\n</code_context>\n<issue_to_address>\n**Negative deliveries are still accepted**\n\nWhen old and new application versions write to the same database during a rolling deployment, or a delivery row is inserted directly into SQLite or by another writer, the check in `schedule` only rejects negative `scheduled_at` values from callers that use that function; SQLite still accepts negative values, and `deliver_due` treats those rows as due and delivers them immediately.\n\nEnforce the non-negative `scheduled_at` rule with a database-level constraint.\n</issue_to_address>\n~~~\n\n</details>\n\n### Sourcery assessment\n\n**Approval pending.** 1 finding to address first.\n\nBlocking findings: `reports.py:24`\n\n***\n\nYour trial expires on December 11, 2026. Please [upgrade](https://app.sourcery.ai/dashboard/billing?connection=github&owner=Swizzle-AI&from_surface=github_bot&intent=trial_upgrade) to continue using Sourcery \u2728\n\n<!--\n<agent_instructions>\nSourcery reviewed this pull request. Handle the review as follows:\n1. Triage every unresolved Sourcery review comment on this pull request: fix the issue, or reply to the comment with the reason you are not fixing it.\n2. Sourcery re-reviews the first 5 pushes to this pull request automatically; 5 automatic re-reviews remain. After each push, wait for the `Sourcery review` check again and read its summary. When a review raises nothing new to fix, you are done.\n</agent_instructions>\n-->",
